kingdom hearts 4 has been announced and  it might include a star wars level  square enix has announced that  development is underway on kingdom  hearts 4 the next entry in the  long-running disney rpg series the news  came as part of a 20th anniversary  celebration event and included the  release of the very first trailer  kingdom hearts 4 kicks off a new  storyline for the franchise the lost  master arc sora returns but he's  sporting a new look the trailer  showcases some brief glimpses of  gameplay as sora squares off against a  giant shadow monster in the middle of a  city street this new location is  quadratum with square enix describes as  a large expansive city set in a gorgeous  realistic world unlike anything ever  seen before in kingdom hearts no further  details were shared on this location or  the overall gameplay or story donald  duck and goofy both return in kingdom  hearts 4 and a new mysterious character  will also be introduced there's no word  on what platforms kingdom hearts 4 will  be available for although kingdom hearts  3 was eventually released for pc xbox  one ps4 and nintendo switch with the  latter being a cloud streaming version  likewise there's no release date either  but fans seem to think square enix's  reveal of the new kingdom hearts may  have teased more than just a regular  crossover with disney's iconic  characters as many of those fans spotted  a brief glimpse of what appears to be  the foot of an all-terrain scout  transport in a location that could be  the forest moon of endor such a  crossover wouldn't be too surprising for  kingdom hearts 4. disney has acquired  more intellectual properties in the  years since kingdom hearts first debuted  such as marvel entertainment in 2009 and  the star wars franchise in 2012. with  avengers spider-man and star wars  characters part of the disney empire the  potential for bigger crossovers in  kingdom hearts 4 is possible over on  twitter fans said things like if we're  really getting a star wars world in  kingdom hearts 4 i can't wait to see  what the heartless designs for that  world will look like been thinking about  kingdom hearts 4 since yesterday and the  idea of star wars heck even marvel  worlds having inclusion in the franchise  considering the tonal shift has me uber  excited for what's to come kingdom  hearts looks cool star wars is a fun  idea but i hope they add shows because  pepper and fighting sephiroth is awesome  in more kingdom hearts news square enix  also announced a new mobile game called  kingdom hearts the missing link which  will have its first closed beta later  this year the gameplay features 3d  rendered environments plenty of  heartless to battle and what appears to  be customizable keyblade masters a  number of disney locations can also be  spotted in the trailer such as the  forest from tangle that was featured in  kingdom hearts 3. square enix added that  the closed beta will roll out later this  year in select regions although those  exact locations have not been revealed  an exact release date for the ios and  android device launch hasn't been nailed  down yet either this isn't the only  kingdom hearts mobile game available as  kingdom hearts dark road has been around  for a few years now square enix revealed  that the grand finale of the kingdom  hearts union x storyline will be  released for free in august let us know  in the comments how excited you are for  kingdom hearts 4 and what worlds you're  hoping to see
 

